{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em] [Em] [C]
[G]I remember the thirty-five sweet [Em]goodbyes
[C]When you put me on the [D]Wolverine up to [G]Annandale
[G]It was still September when your daddy was quite [Em]surprised
[C]To find you with the [D]working girls in the county [G]jail
I was [C]smoking with the boys upstairs
When I [D]heard about the whole affair
I said,  [G]Oh   [Em]no
[G]William and [Em]Mary won't [C]do
Well I did [D]not think the [Am7]girl
Could be   [Bm7]so    [Em7]cruel
And I'm [D]never going [Am7]back
To my   [Bm7]old     [G]school
{end_of_verse}

